From 35058539c17da18fb7b5e04c301d013dbcc6a863 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Angelo Arifi <arifilabs@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 12:06:57 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] feat(r61): hoist the iq3 sign application out of the NUM_COLS
 loop, behind GGML_ARIFI_IQ3_MMVQ

R61 step 0(b) measured the residual per-column select in mul_mat_vec_iq3_s.comp and
mul_mat_vec_iq3_xxs.comp at 88 marginal OpSelect and 1303 / 1226 marginal instructions per
extra column, against mul_mat_vec_iq4_xs.comp's 8 / 333 on a structurally identical shader.
The sign byte and the grid values are A-side only; the lookups were already hoisted, the
APPLICATION was not.

Specialization constant 3 (ARIFI_IQ3_SIGN_HOIST) now selects between the shipped body, kept
verbatim as text so the default arm's codegen is provably the pre-R61 one, and a v2 arm that
applies the sign once per (l, row) and leaves the column body as eight unguarded fmas. Both
arms form the same products and accumulate them through the same fma nest in the same order,
so they are bit-identical; only when the negation is evaluated moves. Default legacy, ONE
binary serves both, and the _id mirror carries the constant too.

Also: GGML_ARIFI_IQ3_N7_ROWS=1|2|4 reshapes the n=7 pipeline's NUM_ROWS alone, to discriminate
the step-0 NUM_COLS==7 runtime cliff (21-26x its neighbours with the instruction count exactly
on the linear trend) from every non-spill hypothesis; unset it is inert. And
GGML_ARIFI_OP_DUMP=<path> appends the test backend's raw outputs for a filtered sweep, so two
arms can be compared by sha256 of the file rather than by tolerance.

No default moved. No route changed. With the three variables unset the engine diff is three
getenv calls at first pipeline creation and nothing else.

Origin: fork-authored (ArifiLabs lane-249 R61 iq3 MMVQ wide-width step 2, Opus 5 MEDIUM kernel-maker)
Measured-effect: op-level perf-mode only (rows in receipts); served t/s UNMEASURED by the maker - HQ pairs quiet
Lane: lane-249
Cherry-picked-from: b32d24006 (SOURCE PATHS ONLY, ArifiLabs lane-254 R66 integration)
Recut-onto: 1b6185951 (ArifiLabs lane-254 R66c, from 201d0b386)
